#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""kiwi-killswitch-settings — GTK4/libadwaita front-end for kiwi-killswitchd.

Talks to the root daemon over the D-Bus system bus. No pkexec, no polkit
prompts: the daemon's bus policy authorizes the `wheel` group, so everything
here is passwordless.

Three things shape this UI:

  * The one thing people come here for is picking WHICH VPN connection is
    protected, so that list is on the front page, not behind a layer of saved
    setups. There is one live configuration, not named profiles.
  * The daemon never starts or stops a VPN. You bring your connections up in
    GNOME Settings; the kill switch builds the firewall around whatever is
    actually alive. The UI says so wherever it matters.
  * Settings are STAGED. Editing a row does not change the firewall — it queues
    a change, and the bar at the bottom applies the whole batch in one atomic
    transaction. That is what makes "reconfigure from LAN+node to tethering+VPN
    while already on tethering, then hit apply" leak-free: there is never a
    half-applied state, and never a disarm in between.
"""
